# Example of PAM for faceauth (see Linux pam_exec(8))
#
# Important: lines in /etc/pam.d/* DO NOT pass through the USER's shell support
# is in progress. I can ask the user.: -what is my name
# I'm not transmitting -you: pam_exec transmits PAM_USER (Linux-PAM) to another user.
#
# auth [success=2 default=ignore] pam_exec.so quiet /usr/local/bin/faceauth-auth
# auth [success=1 default=error] pam_unix.so try_first_pass is reset to zero